# fem-em-solver scheduled automation — see docs/automation/ in the repo.
# 90-minute grid, 16 slots/day: 3 Fable plan reviews (45 min cap) at
# 03:00 / 10:30 / 18:00, each followed by 4 Opus implementer runs (65 min
# hard kill). 01:30–03:00 is left as buffer before the 03:00 review.
# Sunday AND Wednesday 02:15 run the weekly planning review (Fable, high
# effort, 60 min cap) in that buffer slot — twice weekly since 2026-09-01,
# splitting the interval 3/4 days so the long-horizon queue is refilled
# mid-week instead of only at the week boundary. 02:15 is the only buffer
# wide enough for a 60-min session and sits just after the 02:00 usage
# reset. Note: a weekly run that uses its full hour ends at 03:15 and the
# shared flock will make that day's 03:00 daily review skip.
# Sessions never overlap; all runs share one flock. Per-command compute
# stays under the repo's 10-minute tier ceiling.
0 3,18 * * * /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/daily-review.sh
30 10 * * * /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/daily-review.sh
30 4,7,13,16,19,22 * * * /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/implementer-run.sh
0 0,6,9,12,15,21 * * * /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/implementer-run.sh
15 2 * * 0,3 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/weekly-review.sh
# Sunday 01:45: mechanical log-retention sweep (no Claude session; ~1 min),
# in the buffer after the 00:00 implementer slot's 01:05 hard kill and before
# the 02:15 weekly review. See docs/testing/retention-policy.md §4.
45 1 * * 0 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/housekeeping.sh
# 02:00 daily: the XL window, if one is queued in scripts/automation/xl-queue.env
# (operator directive 2026-09-09). No Claude session — an XL window is one
# deterministic command, and running it from an agent is what made it hard: a
# foreground harness call is capped at 660 s and an implementer slot is killed
# at 65 min, so no scheduled *session* can hold a 2 h window; a cron script has
# neither limit. 02:00 is chosen because the box is shared with work this
# sandbox cannot see (the Windows host is unreachable from it), and a quiet
# hour is a better answer than detection that cannot work. It takes its own
# lock, not the automation flock, so a 2 h window cannot starve the 02:15
# weekly or the 03:00 review — both documentation-only. Worst case it ends at
# 04:00, before the 04:30 implementer slot. Exits in a second when nothing is
# queued, which is the normal state.
# 02:00 Sun-Fri: the XL window (2 h, 512 GiB), if one is queued in
# scripts/automation/xl-queue.env. Budget is three per trailing 7 days,
# enforced by the guard against xl-ledger.md, so this entry can fire nightly
# and simply does nothing once the budget is spent or the queue is empty.
0 2 * * 0-5 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/xl-run.sh xl
# 02:00 Saturday: the XXL window (8 h, 754 GiB, one per week), from
# scripts/automation/xxl-queue.env. Saturday is its own day so the two tiers
# cannot both start at 02:00 and contend for the box; 8 h from 02:00 ends at
# 10:00, so it overlaps the 04:30-09:00 implementer slots -- those are 2-8 rank
# jobs and the box is 36 cores, but a Saturday XXL window is the one time the
# machine is deliberately oversubscribed. Operator directive 2026-09-10.
0 2 * * 6 /home/taz5297/Development/fem-em-solver/scripts/automation/xl-run.sh xxl
